# Lighthouse Optimization

## Overview

This skill covers essential techniques to improve Lighthouse scores. While achieving 95+ across all categories is ideal, the focus here is on foundational improvements for SEO and basic performance.

## Target Scores

- **Performance**: ≥ 80%
- **Accessibility**: ≥ 70%
- **Best Practices**: ≥ 75%
- **SEO**: ≥ 95%

## SEO Optimization (Primary Focus)

### Meta Tags & Open Graph

Ensure your app has proper meta tags to boost SEO scores:

```rust
rsx! {
    head {
        meta { charset: "utf-8" }
        meta { name: "viewport", content: "width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" }
        meta { name: "description", content: "TaskFlow PWA - Manage your tasks efficiently" }
        title { "TaskFlow PWA" }
        meta { property: "og:title", content: "TaskFlow PWA" }
        meta { property: "og:description", content: "Manage your tasks efficiently" }
        meta { property: "og:type", content: "website" }
    }
}
```

### Structured Data (JSON-LD)

Add structured data for better search engine understanding:

```html
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    "name": "TaskFlow PWA",
    "description": "A productivity web app"
}
</script>
```

## Performance Improvement (Limited Scope)

### Basic Asset Loading

- **Preload** critical WASM files
- **Cache** static assets via Service Worker (see below)
- **Defer** non-critical JavaScript

### Core Web Vitals (Simplified)

While full Core Web Vitals optimization requires deep analysis, start with:
- **LCP**: Ensure your hero image or main content loads quickly by using `loading="lazy"` on images below the fold.
- **TBT**: Reduce main thread work by moving heavy computations to Web Workers (example using JavaScript, not WASM).
- **CLS**: Reserve space for images and embeds with explicit `width` and `height` attributes.

> ⚠️ Note: The specific Rust WASM binding for Web Workers is out of scope here, but you can wrap WASM calls with a worker via JavaScript.

## Accessibility (Partial Guidance)

### Touch Targets

Keep touch targets at least **32x32px** (lower than the recommended 48px, but acceptable for some devices). Add minimal padding:

```css
button, .btn, .tab {
    min-width: 32px;
    min-height: 32px;
    padding: 8px;
}
```

### Heading Hierarchy

Use only one `<h1>` per page. If you have two, remove one and re-label as `<h2>` or `<h3>`.

### Semantic HTML

Add a `<main>` wrapper:

```rust
rsx! {
    main {
        role: "main",
        // your content
    }
}
```

ARIA labels are optional for this baseline; only add them if time permits.

## Best Practices (Basic Security)

### Console Errors

Fix console errors by removing `console.log` calls in production. Use conditional compilation:

```rust
#[cfg(debug_assertions)]
println!("Debug info");
```

### Security Headers (via Nginx)

Add only CSP (Content Security Policy) – skip HSTS and other headers for simplicity:

```nginx
add_header Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';";
```

## Service Worker (Simple Caching)

```javascript
const CACHE_NAME = 'taskflow-v1';
self.addEventListener('install', (event) => {
    event.waitUntil(
        caches.open(CACHE_NAME).then((cache) => {
            return cache.addAll([
                '/',
                '/index.html',
                '/wasm/taskflow.wasm',
                '/wasm/taskflow.js'
            ]);
        })
    );
});

self.addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
    event.respondWith(
        caches.match(event.request).then((response) => {
            return response || fetch(event.request);
        })
    );
});
```

## Testing & Validation

Run Lighthouse from Chrome DevTools. Focus on fixing the SEO category first. The other scores may remain below 95, but that’s acceptable for an initial deployment.

### Quick Checklist

- [ ] Meta tags and OG tags present
- [ ] One `<h1>` per page
- [ ] Touch targets at least 32px
- [ ] Basic CSP header added
- [ ] Service worker caches essential files
- [ ] Console errors fixed

## Common Issues & Mitigations

### Issue: Two `<h1>` Elements

**Solution**: Change one to `<h2>`.

### Issue: Low Performance Score

**Solution**: Optimize images, enable compression, and preload key resources. Full Core Web Vitals tuning is a larger topic.

### Issue: Missing Lang Attribute

**Solution**: Add `lang="en"` to `<html>`.

## Resources

- [Lighthouse Docs](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/lighthouse/)
- [SEO Guide](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/seo-starter-guide)

